    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d22e3090_4e33f399",
        "filename": "common/usb_charger_bd99955.c",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 173,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-05-07T00:34:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think BC1.2 detection should work independently of other detection methods, if possible. Even with this code, we may not realize we have a PD / type-C charger yet, and do detection anyway. Is there any harm to always doing BC1.2 detection on attach?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 172,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 173,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "ea343ee56901268b26b39cc76fcee1e6dd0ca3e2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d22e3090_11050c69",
        "filename": "common/usb_charger_bd99955.c",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 173,
      "author": {
        "id": 1128369
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-05-07T00:53:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For both PD \u0026 BC1.2 VBUS interrupt is same so it is not possible to find for which type detach event occurred. So added code get_charge_supplier() to get the information before the detach occurs. If type is PD (or already PD detected) then we don\u0027t see BC1.2 detected so we can skip checking for BC1.2.",
      "parentUuid": "d22e3090_4e33f399",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 172,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 173,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "ea343ee56901268b26b39cc76fcee1e6dd0ca3e2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d22e3090_b155180e",
        "filename": "common/usb_charger_bd99955.c",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 173,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-05-07T01:34:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we get a VBUS interrupt, several things should kick off -- the PD task will try to determine if a PD charger is attached. The USB charger task will try to identify a BC1.2 charge port attached. Some other task (actually, usually our VBUS interrupt) will tell charge manager about the existence of VBUS. Based on these independent inputs, charge manager will make a decision about the charge port / current limit to select.\n\nWhat does skipping BC1.2 detection gain us? It violates the division of labor I mentioned above. And, it needs to work even when a PD port is attached, even if we don\u0027t change the code, because:\n\n- PD negotiation may be slow, we might not see a PD / type-C charger yet and\n- The way you wrote get_charge_supplier, for the non-active port, you will always do BC1.2 detection.\n\nI don\u0027t see the benefit of skipping BC1.2 detection and I\u0027m worried it will create bugs.",
      "parentUuid": "d22e3090_11050c69",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 172,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 173,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "ea343ee56901268b26b39cc76fcee1e6dd0ca3e2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
